# P1 · Front desk and appointments MVP · Weeks 4–10 · R1 Front Desk
# exit: 1 two clinics 2 consecutive weeks real bookings no paper · 2 0 double bookings at 100 parallel · 3 median check-in ≤ 60 s · 4 ≥ 98 % reminders delivered, failures visible · 5 no open high/critical findings
# nfr:  1 booking p95 < 300 ms, calendar first render < 2.5 s on 4G · 2 Hangfire on PostgreSQL, no Redis/Service Bus · 3 tablet-responsive reception
# pkg:  1 production tenant per clinic · 2 30-min reception training + desk card · 3 support channel with named contact · 4 baseline metrics
# dep:  1 privacy notice + consent wording reviewed (DPDP/UAE) · 2 DLT SMS sender + templates · 3 two partner clinics signed

@epic MDV-P1-E01 | Public site | P1-01 | Landing, region/residency selector, trust centre and demo request on the Razor public site.
@epic MDV-P1-E02 | Clinic onboarding and practice settings | P1-02, P1-12 | A clinic or hospital applies through an onboarding request (ADR-016) and, once approved, sets up the practice, hours, holidays, notifications and legal terms.
@epic MDV-P1-E03 | Doctors, staff and staff lifecycle | P1-03, P1-11 | Owners add doctors (licence they attest, signature, schedule) and staff (roles, scope); access ends immediately on offboarding.
@epic MDV-P1-E04 | Schedules and availability | P1-04 | Working hours, breaks, slot lengths, leave and exceptions per doctor and location.
@epic MDV-P1-E05 | Patient registration, duplicates and consents | P1-05, P1-12 | Register India and UAE patients quickly and safely, with separate versioned consents and no silent duplicates.
@epic MDV-P1-E06 | Booking and no double booking | P1-06, P1-07 | Create, move, cancel and track appointments with database-guaranteed slot integrity.
@epic MDV-P1-E07 | Reception board and queue | P1-08 | Run the waiting room: check-in, statuses, call/room, multi-doctor overview and TV display.
@epic MDV-P1-E08 | Confirmations, reminders and notification centre | P1-09 | Email/SMS confirmations and reminders with delivery status; in-app notification centre.
@epic MDV-P1-E09 | Practice access log | P1-10 | Owners see who opened which record and when.
@epic MDV-P1-E10 | Pilot readiness and R1 gate | P1-01, P1-12 | External dependencies, production tenants, training, baselines, security review and the R1 exit gate.
@epic MDV-P1-E11 | Connectivity and resilience | P1-06, P1-08 | The desk keeps working on flaky Indian connections: safe retries, timeouts, offline assets and a paper fallback; nothing with patient data is stored in the browser without a decision.

=== MDV-P1-001
status: Done
progress:
- [PR #52](https://github.com/ALFRED-LUCIFER/medvya/pull/52): Razor Pages in Host.Api/PublicSite — F-01 landing (exact copy, two CTAs, three pillars) and pricing placeholder; no JavaScript, no third-party resources or fonts; copy from packages/i18n, colours from packages/ui tokens (embedded at build)
- Region switch India/UAE is a plain link storing only the region code in an HttpOnly preference cookie; English, Hindi (/hi) and Arabic (/ar, RTL) with hreflang, canonical and description; public endpoints run before authentication so the session cookie is never read (probe test, mutation-checked)
- Verified in the browser (axe clean at 360/640/1280 px in en/hi/ar, keyboard path, no-JS region switch, RTL); Lighthouse mobile 100/100 performance/accessibility on /, /ar and /hi/pricing (local)
- Review fixes ([PR #67](https://github.com/ALFRED-LUCIFER/medvya/pull/67)): 44 px targets for region, nav and language links with an underline on the current region; anti-forgery cookie Secure over HTTPS; pages sent no-cache, no-store; tests cover every page (no script, session never read, no certification claim when rendered)
- Left: product shot and favicon assets (design); own host name for the site when App Service hosting lands (MDV-P0-007); /region and /trust links go live with MDV-P1-002 and MDV-P1-003
