sources: docs/02-design/source/Medvya Access and Onboarding (F-01); docs/02-design/screen-specs.md#f-01-landing
desc:
Server-rendered Razor Pages in Host.Api/PublicSite (no patient data). Nav: For doctors · For hospitals · Trust centre · Pricing (placeholder) · region switch India/UAE · Sign in. Hero "Talk to your patient. Medvya writes the note. You approve it." with exactly two CTAs: "I'm a doctor · start free trial" → onboarding (F-04), "For hospitals · book a demo" → demo request (F-07). Region switch changes hero tag, languages and residency line. Three pillars.
ac:
- The landing page renders without JavaScript, scores ≥ 90 on Lighthouse performance and accessibility on mobile.
- Region switch India/UAE changes the hero tag, language list and residency line exactly as in screen-specs F-01, and is remembered via a non-tracking cookie.
- Only the two designed CTAs exist above the fold; Pricing shows a placeholder with no invented prices or metrics.
- Pages are available in English, Hindi and Arabic (RTL) with SEO metadata and no third-party trackers without consent.
- No PHI or tenant data is reachable from public pages (separate route group, no auth cookie read).
notes:
- Scope change, ADR-016 (docs/adr/ADR-016-organisation-onboarding-and-approval.md, owner decision 10 Nov 2026): there is no solo-doctor account. The doctor CTA reads "Register your clinic" and goes to the onboarding request (MDV-P1-062); the hospital CTA stays "book a demo" until Hospital onboarding opens in the same request.

