status: Partly done
progress:
- [PR #56](https://github.com/ALFRED-LUCIFER/medvya/pull/56) (stacked on #57): /region with the designed copy and India/UAE cards (no JavaScript); "Continue in {region}" goes to that country's own sign-up address (PublicSite:Deployments:SignUpUrls) or, if the country is not live, to a waitlist (contact fields only) stored in the Leads module
- Tenant.CountryCode and ResidencyRegion are init-only and EF throws on any later change (domain, EF and SQL Server tests, mutation-checked); copy translated (en/hi/ar); browser-verified (axe clean, keyboard, RTL); Lighthouse mobile 100 (local)
- Review fixes ([PR #67](https://github.com/ALFRED-LUCIFER/medvya/pull/67)): waitlist refuses control characters in the name and has its own anti-forgery test; the form quota counts an IPv6 subscriber (/64), not each address
- Privacy notice and consent ([PR #75](https://github.com/ALFRED-LUCIFER/medvya/pull/75)): the waitlist shows a notice above the submit button (who, itemised fields, purpose, no sharing or other use, 2 years then deleted, how to withdraw or ask for deletion, the Data Protection Board of India or UAE Data Office) and a required, unticked consent box; refused on the server without it (consent_required); stores ConsentedAt (UTC) and NoticeVersion; no form without PublicSite:PrivacyContact
- Onboarding (MDV-P1-004): the selection is recorded in the audit trail when the tenant is created (action onboarding.complete.IN or .AE) and the new tenant's country is checked against the deployment (Onboarding:DeploymentCountry)
- Left: configure the live country's sign-up address once onboarding and the launch deployment exist (MDV-P0-003, MDV-P0-007); the real privacy contact address and counsel-reviewed notice wording (MDV-P1-044)
