desc:
Notifications tab: which events send messages (booking confirmation, 24 h reminder, 2 h reminder, cancellation), channels enabled (email, SMS; WhatsApp placeholder for P4), sender name, quiet hours, template preview (no clinical details). Data tab: tenant country and residency (read-only), export placeholder (P5), retention defaults (read-only labels), link to access log (F-12).
ac:
- Turning off a reminder type stops future scheduling of that reminder (already-queued ones are cancelled).
- Template previews show placeholders only; templates cannot include clinical fields (validation rejects clinical merge fields).
- Quiet hours prevent SMS sending inside the window (job reschedules to the window end).
- Residency and country are displayed read-only with the trust-centre wording.

=== MDV-P1-007
status: Done
progress:
- Merged [PR #685](https://github.com/ALFRED-LUCIFER/medvya/pull/685): Settings -> Doctors tab with the seven-step Add doctor wizard (details, licence, verification status, schedule hint, default fees, access, signature image). One transaction creates the Invited hospital-doctor membership, DoctorProfile, DoctorLicence (pending) and the P0-013 invitation (emailed); licence rules reuse OnboardingRules per country plus category and a future expiry date. `/v1/settings/doctors/*` needs practice configuration; licence verify/reject is NOT a practice capability: `POST /v1/operations/licences/{tenantId}/{doctorId}/decision` needs the Medvya operations capability (staff ids in `Operations:LicenceReviewers`), runs inside the licence's tenant, records verified_by/verified_at, audits licence.verify / licence.reject in the same transaction and, on rejection, needs a reason, emails the practice contact address and shows the reason on the Doctors tab (the owner can correct and resubmit). The server gate now also holds a doctor with no licence row (mutation-checked: practice admin cannot verify; pending, rejected and never-submitted doctors get no ClinicalNotes access). Signature image: PNG/JPEG by file signature, 512 KB, private Blob under a random key, no read endpoint (printed prescriptions only), UI states the passkey / MFA sentence. EN/HI/AR, RTL, axe clean at 768 px
- DEFAULT DECISION (founder has not decided; change here when they do): verification is done by Medvya operations only, no owner attestation. Open question: who checks which register (NMC / state council, DoH / DHA / MOHAP) and the SLA ("usually within 1 working day" is shown to doctors but unmeasured)
- Left: a back-office screen and cross-tenant pending queue (operations get tenant and doctor ids out of band; needs a reviewed read path inside row-level security); operations role from the identity provider instead of a configured id list (MDV-P0-011); certificate file upload (only its name is kept; Blob upload path); malware scan of the signature image (with MDV-P0-006); printing the signature on prescriptions (P2); one facility per doctor (multi-facility scope with MDV-P1-009); expiry reminders and blocking on an expired licence; category is free text (no per-authority list); the sign-up wizard still collects no category or expiry
