confidence: 70 | Wizard steps and signature rule are designed; the data script for the wizard was truncated and the licence verification back-office process is not yet defined (P2 dependency).
sources: docs/02-design/source/Medvya Clinician App (Add doctor); docs/02-design/screen-specs.md#practice-settings-f-08--f-12--medvya-clinician-app--data-truncated-labels-only; PRD v2 P2 dependency "Doctor licence verification process defined"
desc:
Settings → Doctors → Add doctor wizard: details (name, specialty, qualifications, languages) → licence (country, authority: state medical council/NMC or DoH/DHA/MOHAP, number, category, expiry, certificate upload) → verification (status pending/verified/rejected, verified_by, verified_at; done by Medvya operations or owner attestation per policy) → schedule (link to MDV-P1-011) → fees (default consultation fees; full services in P4) → access (role and facility scope) → signature (drawn or uploaded image; optional clinic stamp). Creates CLINICIAN_PROFILE and CLINICIAN_LICENCE and sends an invitation.
ac:
- A doctor cannot record or sign until licence status is Verified; the restriction is enforced server-side.
- Licence number format is validated per authority where a format is known; expiry date is required.
- The verification decision records who verified and when, and is audited; rejected licences notify the owner with the reason.
- The signature image is stored privately and appears only on printed prescriptions; the UI states "Signing in Medvya is always an authenticated action by the doctor (passkey / MFA), never the image alone."
- The new doctor appears in schedule columns once hours are set.
notes:
- Define the licence verification process (who checks which register, SLA "usually within 1 working day") with the founder; this closes the P2 dependency.
- Superseded in scope by ADR-016 (docs/adr/ADR-016-organisation-onboarding-and-approval.md, owner decision 10 Nov 2026): Medvya operations no longer verify doctors. Owner attestation replaces the Verified/Pending states and the licence gate (MDV-P1-065); the licence verify and reject endpoint and Operations:LicenceReviewers are replaced by organisation approval (MDV-P1-064). The Done work stays until those tickets land.

