sources: PRD v2 P1-05; docs/02-design/screen-specs.md#global-search-d-02
desc:
Search by name, MRN, phone, ABHA/EID (exact). Results show the full name, age, sex and the MRN and phone tails (MDV-AUDIT-1100, a product decision of 13 Nov 2026: staff who register and book can see the name; the doctor's ⌘K lookup still shows initials); the rest of the record needs it opened, which is audited with purpose "registration/booking". Directory list with filters (incomplete registration, recently registered) and pagination. Blind-index (HMAC) columns support exact ID lookups.
ac:
- Searching by full phone number or exact EID/ABHA returns the matching patient(s); partial ID search is not allowed.
- Result rows show the full name, age, sex and MRN and phone tails (never the whole phone, birth date or identifiers); full demographics appear only after opening, which writes an audit event.
- Empty state: "No patients match. Register a new patient".
- Search p95 < 300 ms with 50,000 synthetic patients; endpoint rate-limited.

=== MDV-P1-019
status: Partly done
progress:
- Merged [PR #678](https://github.com/ALFRED-LUCIFER/medvya/pull/678): patient consents at registration. Consents step (full mode; quick mode shows treatment only): treatment locked on, reminders per channel (WhatsApp, SMS), link to ABHA (India) / HIE named from the emirate (UAE), portal (on, invite in P4), health tips & offers (off); each decision, declined ones too, is a CONSENT_RECEIPT (type, channel, policy version, jurisdiction `IN` / `AE-<emirate>`, decision, time, staff actor) in `patients.ConsentReceipts`, an append-only SQL ledger table (UPDATE and DELETE rejected, tested) with RLS, written in the registration's own transaction
- Registration without treatment consent, or with a stale wording version, is refused (400) and saves nothing (SAFETY test, mutation-checked); `POST /v1/patients/{id}/consents` records a changed decision as a new receipt, history kept, audited, active facility only (another facility 404, nothing written)
- Reminders (MDV-P1-032/033) ask `IPatientConsents.IsGrantedAsync(patientId, type, channel)` in `Medvya.Patients.Application` (channels WhatsApp, SMS, email): the newest receipt decides, a tie counts as withdrawn, no receipt means no consent. The host implements the Notifications module's `IReminderConsent` on it (`PatientReminderConsent`, tested: no receipt no send, a grant sends, a withdrawal stops it, mutation-checked); en/hi/ar, axe clean, 44 px rows, 768 px and Arabic RTL, real-API browser check
- Left: legally reviewed wording and per-tenant published privacy notice versions (MDV-P1-044; wording is a marked DRAFT, `ConsentPolicy.CurrentVersion` / `consents` in registration.ts, shortcut recorded); tenant-level ToS and DPA acceptance and "owners cannot activate the production tenant before it" (no activation step exists yet, needs its own change in Tenancy); a screen to change a consent from the record (API ready; portal R-03 in P4)
title: Legal terms and separate versioned consents at registration (treatment, reminders per channel, sharing, portal, marketing)
type: Story
epic: MDV-P1-E05
prd: P1-12
screens: P-02, F-08
covers: dep:1
priority: MUST
roles: Receptionist, Practice owner
labels: consent, legal, compliance
estimate: 3
weeks: 6-7
depends: MDV-P1-013, MDV-P1-044
confidence: 75 | Consent UI and receipt model are designed; final wording depends on the DPDP/UAE legal review (dependency 1).
sources: PRD v2 P1-12; docs/02-design/source/Medvya Patient Registration (Consents step); docs/04-security-compliance/README.md#consent-model-separate-versioned-receipts
desc:
Tenant level: owner accepts Medvya Terms of Service and the clinic Data Processing Agreement during onboarding; the clinic privacy notice is published (versioned). Patient level (Consents step): treatment (required, locked), reminders on WhatsApp/SMS (per channel), link to ABHA (India) / HIE (UAE, per emirate), portal access (invite in P4), health tips & offers (off by default). Each decision stores CONSENT_RECEIPT with consent_type, policy_version, jurisdiction, decision, decided_at, channel and actor. Recording consent is NOT asked here (per-visit, P3).
ac:
- Every consent is a separate toggle; marketing defaults off; treatment is required and cannot be toggled off.
- Each decision creates an immutable receipt (ledger) with policy version and jurisdiction; changing a decision creates a new receipt and keeps history.
- The privacy notice version shown at registration is the currently published one; publishing a new version does not alter old receipts.
- Activation is one accepted-terms record on the tenant (terms version, timestamp, who accepted): until it exists, the production tenant cannot book appointments or send messages; accepting it records all three (decision 5 Nov 2026, built on the draft wording).
- Reminder sending (MDV-P1-032/033) checks the channel consent before every send (test).
- Final wording is the legally reviewed text from MDV-P1-044 in en/hi/ar.

=== MDV-P1-020
status: Done
progress:
