confidence: 90 | Mechanism fully specified by PRD v2; test is explicit in the exit gate.
sources: PRD v2 P1-07, exit 2; docs/03-architecture/data-model.md#key-constraints
desc:
Filtered unique index on (doctor_id, location_id, slot_start) for non-cancelled appointments; booking inside a transaction holding pg_advisory_xact_lock on "doctor:{id}:{date}"; the frontend check is only a convenience. Multi-slot visits reserve every covered slot.
ac:
- An automated test fires 100 parallel booking attempts at one slot; exactly one succeeds and 99 receive a clear "slot no longer available" error (exit gate 2), on Testcontainers PostgreSQL and on staging.
- Overlapping multi-slot bookings are rejected the same way.
- Deadlocks/lock timeouts are retried safely without creating duplicates.
- The test runs in CI on every PR touching Scheduling.

