sources: docs/02-design/source/Medvya Clinical Screens (P-05 Queue TV display); docs/02-design/source/Medvya Gap Analysis (Queue and token screen)
desc:
Tokens issued at check-in (prefix per doctor/room, e.g. A-07). TV route /queue/tv?display=… authenticated by a device display token (no user login) shows "Now: token · room · doctor" and "Next: token · ≈ wait". Large type, high contrast, auto-refresh via SignalR, works on a basic smart-TV browser.
ac:
- The TV payload contains tokens, rooms, doctor display names and waits only; no patient names, MRNs or reasons (API contract test).
- Display tokens are revocable and scoped to one facility.
- Calling a patient updates the TV within 2 seconds and optionally plays a chime.
- Layout is readable at 3 metres (minimum 48px token text) and in Arabic/English.

=== MDV-P1-032
status: Partly done
progress:
- Notifications module (`src/Modules/Notifications`): NOTIFICATION / NOTIFICATION_ATTEMPT (status, attempts, backoff, provider reference, short failure code; no message text or address stored), EF filters + RLS, role `medvya_notifications`; Scheduling's outbox is published by `OutboxDispatcher` to `IAppointmentSubscriber`s (at least once, in order); a trigger keeps the tenants that wrote events so the job knows whose scope to enter
- Hangfire on Azure SQL in schema `hangfire` (no Redis/Service Bus): one recurring job publishes each tenant's outbox then sends what is due (confirmation within about a minute); read-only dashboard at `/admin/jobs` only for users listed in `Jobs:DashboardUsers` (nobody by default); jobs off unless `Jobs:Enabled`
- Booking queues a confirmation and the 24 h / 2 h reminders (facility time, quiet hours 21:00-08:00 moved to the end); reschedule/cancel cancels queued messages and sends the right message once (idempotent on the event id); walk-ins get nothing; consent checked at send time through `IReminderConsent` (default denies all until MDV-P1-019 supplies the real one); retries with backoff (1, 5, 30 min) up to 4 tries then Failed; templates en/hi/ar with clinic, date and time only
- Reception sees each message's status on the appointment panel (`GET /v1/appointments/{id}/notifications`, audited, view membership at the facility) and `GET /v1/notifications/delivery` lists per-channel counts and every failure with its code
- Tested on SQL Server (17 tests + signature/auth tests); mutation-checked: consent check removed, DLT template id check removed, cancel-on-change removed, address added to the body
- Left: the real consent source (MDV-P1-019); the SendGrid event webhook parser and its ECDSA signature check (receipts take a normalised body signed with HMAC for now; email goes over SendGrid's SMTP relay); the Hangfire server in its own Worker.Jobs host and its own database user; failed messages on the board and in the notification centre (MDV-P1-034); the install of Hangfire's tables on deploy (MDV-P0-007); per-clinic quiet hours; Hindi and Arabic wording reviewed by a native speaker
title: Email confirmations and 24 h / 2 h reminders via SendGrid and Hangfire
type: Story
epic: MDV-P1-E08
prd: P1-09
covers: nfr:2, exit:4
priority: MUST
roles: Patient, Receptionist
labels: notifications, jobs
estimate: 2.5
weeks: 7-8
depends: MDV-P1-021, MDV-P1-019
confidence: 86 | Stack decided (Hangfire on PostgreSQL, ACS); template rules defined.
sources: PRD v2 P1-09, P1 NFR 2; docs/03-architecture/integrations.md
desc:
Hangfire server (Worker.Jobs) on PostgreSQL in its own schema/user — no Redis or Service Bus in P1. Email provider: SendGrid (founder decision 20 Oct 2026, free tier) behind the Notifications adapter; Azure Communication Services remains an alternative. Events: booking confirmation, reschedule, cancellation, 24 h and 2 h reminders, leave rebooking. Templates per tenant/language without clinical details. NOTIFICATION and NOTIFICATION_ATTEMPT record provider id, delivery state and retries with backoff; reminders are cancelled when the appointment changes.
ac:
- Booking triggers a confirmation within 1 minute; reminders are sent at 24 h and 2 h before (facility time), respecting quiet hours and channel consent.
- Rescheduling or cancelling cancels pending reminders and sends the right message once (idempotency test).
- Delivery status (queued, sent, delivered, failed, bounced) is stored and visible to reception for each appointment.
- Failed sends are retried with backoff up to the configured limit and then shown as failed on the board/notification centre.
- Hangfire dashboard is only reachable by Medvya operations through authenticated admin route; no Redis or Service Bus resources exist in P1 infrastructure.

=== MDV-P1-033
status: Partly done
progress:
- SMS behind `ISmsGateway`: local sink to the mail sink (Development) and a gateway that fails closed (visible as failed) until the provider is chosen (Q-03, MDV-P1-045)
- SMS uses only registered templates: the text must match a catalogue template (`{#var#}` slots, 30 characters each) and in India have its DLT template id from config (`Notifications:Sms:DltTemplateIds`, keys like `Confirmation.en`) and a sender (`Notifications:Sms:Senders` per tenant or `DefaultSender`); otherwise it is Failed at once and never handed to a provider; messages hold no clinical details
- Delivery receipts: `POST /v1/notifications/receipts` (public, HMAC-SHA256 of the body with `Notifications:ReceiptSecret`, refused when unset), applied inside the tenant named by the reference; duplicate and out-of-order receipts are ignored; failures visible to reception (see MDV-P1-032)
- Left: the SMS provider adapter and its own receipt format (Q-03); DLT sender and template registration with the operator (MDV-P1-045, a person task: put the ids in config); delivery-rate dashboard screen (the API returns per-channel counts and every failure; MDV-P1-041); SMS invitations in onboarding step 6
