=== MDV-P1-051
title: Encrypted read-only schedule cache for outages (needs an ADR first)
type: Story
epic: MDV-P1-E11
prd: P1-08
covers: nfr:3
priority: COULD
roles: Receptionist
labels: resilience, connectivity, security
estimate: 5
weeks: 13
depends: MDV-P1-050
confidence: 55 | Storing any patient data in the browser needs a recorded decision; build only if pilot clinics report outages long enough that a paper sheet is not enough.
sources: docs/03-architecture/india-connectivity-power.md section 6(b); deferred 5 Nov 2026
desc:
Show today's schedule read-only, labelled "as of <time>", when the network drops, from a per-user encrypted cache that expires after 12 hours and is wiped on sign-out or deactivation. No search; create, edit and cancel stay disabled. Requires an ADR (what may be stored in the browser, key handling) before any code; not to be built unless pilots show the printed day sheet is not enough.
ac:
- An ADR records what is stored, how it is keyed and why, and is accepted before implementation.
- During an outage the schedule is shown read-only with an "as of" label and create, edit and cancel are disabled.
- The cache is deleted on sign-out, after 12 hours and when the account is deactivated.
- Inspecting the browser store shows only ciphertext, and the test fails if the encryption is removed (mutation check).

