confidence: 70 | Designed in Medvya Web (6 Nov 2026, area auth). Email code, passkey, MFA and recovery run on the Entra pages; this ticket owns the Medvya screens around them.
sources: docs/02-design/source/Medvya Web.dc.html (6 Nov 2026 revamp) (sign in, create account, invitation, choose location, signed out)
desc:
The Medvya-owned screens of the 6 Nov sign-in flow in web/clinic, in the designed two-panel frame (brand panel, help, language, region line): Sign in (work email, "This is a shared computer", continue, passkey and single sign-on entry), which starts the Entra sign-in with the email as a login hint; Create account step 1 (practice type, name, city) and step 2 (name, email, mobile, "I'm the doctor" / "I manage the clinic"), which feed the existing sign-up (MDV-P1-004) before the Entra account is made; invitation acceptance (what the role can and cannot see, full name, expiry); choose location (last used first, signed in as, not you); and signed out / session ended. The email code, MFA set-up and recovery codes are Entra pages and are branded in MDV-P1-060. No password, code or factor is ever handled by Medvya.
ac:
- Given a staff member enters their email, when they continue, then the browser goes to the Entra sign-in with the email as login hint and Medvya stores nothing about it.
- Given "This is a shared computer" is chosen, when the session starts, then it uses the shared-device idle lock and maximum session the server already enforces, decided on the server.
- Given an expired or revoked invitation, when it is opened, then the screen says so and offers to ask the practice for a new one; no account is created.
- Given a user with several locations, when they sign in, then the last used location is listed first and choosing one sets the server-side facility.
- Every screen is keyboard-complete with visible focus, announced errors and 44 px targets; axe is clean in en, hi and ar; Arabic is right to left.

